"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2751,"**
Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm, narrated to us Abū ʿĀṣim, from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Sulaymān al-Aḥwal, that Ṭāwūs informed him that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) passed by a man who was circumambulating the Kaʿbah while leading another man by a nose-ring. So the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) cut it off and then ordered him to lead him by his hand.

He (Ṭāwūs) said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) also passed by a man who was circumambulating the Kaʿbah while leading another man by a strap or a thread or something similar. So the Prophet (ﷺ) cut it off and said, ""Lead him by his hand."""
2752,"**
Narrated to us Sulayman al-Aḥwal who said: All of them [the narrators] informed me that Ṭāwūs informed him that Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) said that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:
*""Indeed, there is a concession in speaking during the Tawāf when there is a need.""*

Abū Bakr [al-Bukhārī] (RA) said: ""This narration indicates the allowance of speaking during the Tawāf when there is a need or necessity."""
